0..78 Comment "//! The data subject\'s shared declarations, written once and imported by every"
79..157 Comment "//! source that reads them (`import \"./data-base.gandr\";`): the free naturals,"
158..238 Comment "//! their addition and the numerals two and three, the integers presented by two"
239..317 Comment "//! cancelling constructors, a three-colour enumeration, the two branches of a"
318..394 Comment "//! binary node and the polymorphic lists. A data block is an inductive type"
395..475 Comment "//! given by its constructors [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory], and a"
476..523 Comment "//! rule between constructor terms quotients it"
524..602 Comment "//! [Altenkirch-2018-quotient_inductive_inductive_types]. The universe subject"
603..657 Comment "//! reads the naturals and the branches from here too."
658..661 Comment "//!"
662..727 Comment "//! - cites: [Altenkirch-2018-quotient_inductive_inductive_types]"
728..784 Comment "//! - cites: [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory]"
785..788 Comment "//!"
789..947 Comment "//! [Altenkirch-2018-quotient_inductive_inductive_types]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-89366-2_16 \"Altenkirch et al., Quotient inductive-inductive types\""
948..1120 Comment "//! [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory]: https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf \"Martin-Löf, Intuitionistic Type Theory\""
